[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3385485449","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111358#issuecomment-3385485449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111358","id":3385485449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JymiJ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T11:42:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T11:42:12Z","body":"> Makes sense to me, but it's worth noting that (like any removal of APIs from headers) this breaks compatibility for thirdparty modules or platforms and user forks who may make use of it.\r\n> \r\n> I'm starting to think that we may need to collect information on all those changes to core headers done recently to add to a subpage of the 4.6 migration guide for C++ engine modifications.\r\n\r\nIt would be possible to add a `[[deprecated]]` version of the removed structures, which would save modules from compile issues. Should I add it?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3385485449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3386832064","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111358#issuecomment-3386832064","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111358","id":3386832064,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J3vTA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T17:18:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T17:19:47Z","body":"Ehh, I don't think that's necessary. Though if you *really* want to have some contingency, appending this to the end of `variant.h` would suffice:\r\n```cpp\r\n#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\r\n// Compatibility with pre-4.6 modules.\r\nusing VariantHasher = HashMapHasherDefault<Variant>;\r\nusing VariantComparator = HashMapComparatorDefault<Variant>;\r\n#endif // DISABLE_DEPRECATED\r\n```\r\nSee also: an [equivalent implementation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/295e465fe403954911ca75145cc5d21546274262/core/version.h#L90-L111) in `version.